WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.000 --> 00:00:09.574
Watch the video unfold, one frame at a time.

2
00:00:09.574 --> 00:00:15.589
Record the change in stride and position as the character moves along the stone path.

3
00:00:15.589 --> 00:00:19.582
Ask which road the character took as the video keeps moving.

4
00:00:19.582 --> 00:00:22.006
The character took the right-hand path.

5
00:00:22.006 --> 00:00:29.657
In the park, the camera reveals people and objects across the scene.

6
00:00:29.657 --> 00:00:35.643
Retain the changing view while keeping earlier observations available.

7
00:00:35.643 --> 00:00:41.644
Working memory retains the scene descriptions and visual changes.

8
00:00:41.644 --> 00:00:45.648
Ask where the sandals were, while the video continues playing.

9
00:00:45.648 --> 00:00:47.732
The sandals were on the ground.

10
00:00:47.732 --> 00:00:54.324
The final example asks about two people seen earlier.

11
00:00:54.324 --> 00:01:00.324
Browse the full history, from working details to episode summaries.

12
00:01:00.324 --> 00:01:04.323
Working memory retains the scene descriptions and visual changes.

13
00:01:04.323 --> 00:01:08.325
Episodes connect observations across time; pins keep facts and guidance available.

14
00:01:08.325 --> 00:01:12.330
The question guides the search for their relative positions.

15
00:01:12.330 --> 00:01:13.599
They were standing side by side.

16
00:01:13.626 --> 00:01:25.600
DeltaStreamer compares consecutive sampled frames, recording what is visible and what changed.

17
00:01:25.600 --> 00:01:37.600
Observations form a hierarchy of working records, episodes, and pins, with links back to their source evidence.

18
00:01:37.600 --> 00:01:49.600
A persistent plan guides retrieval and continued observation. When visual details are missing, the agent can revisit earlier frames.
